## Where docs live

- **`wiki/`** (repo root) holds feature design docs and user guides as UPPERCASE-KEBAB markdown files. Examples are `DESIGN-BLOCKBASED-THERAPY-APPOINTMENT-BOOKING.md`, `BLOCK-APPOINTMENT-BOOKING-USAGE.md`, `PATIENT-DUPLICATE.md`, `PATIENT-DUPLICATE-CHECKER-USAGE-DOC.md`, `insurance-parity-report.md`, and an implementation plan for FHIR terminology parity. Images sit beside them.
  - User guides start with an Introduction, then "This guide covers" bullets, a Quick Start, tables, and step-by-step `### Step N` sections using bold Desk navigation (**Healthcare > Patient Appointment**).
  - Design docs are written separately from usage docs.
- **`README.md`** links to the external documentation at DeepWiki, the Telegram group and install steps. It also contains a Build-managed "Guides" block that lists `.build/RULES.md` and `.build/guides/*`.
- `patient_portal/README.md` covers the SPA.
- `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` / `.build/RULES.md` hold the AI-agent workflow rules.

## PR documentation gate (inherited from upstream)

- `docs_checker.yml` fails `feat:` PRs unless the body links a `/wiki` URL on `biograph.frappe.cloud` / `biograph.io`, or contains `no-docs` or `backport`.
- It queries the upstream `earthians/biograph` API, so on this fork include `no-docs` or a wiki link in `feat` PR bodies.
